{"availability":"available","full":"yesint/molar_vis","name":"molar_vis","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":62,"forks":3,"created":"2026-06-13T13:49:47Z","updated":"2026-10-09T19:16:25Z","license":"Artistic-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://yesint.github.io/molar_vis/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.296Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.296Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.296Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.296Z","stars":62,"forks":3}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A modern, legacy-free molecular visualizer modeled after VMD, written in pure Rust. The molecule is drawn with hand-written GPU ray-cast impostors (WGSL) and real-time cartoon ribbons — no OpenGL fixed pipeline, no X11, no C/C++/Tcl. It runs natively on Linux, Windows, macOS and compiles to WebAssembly (try it now online).","The binary is called molarvis. It is built on molar — a Rust molecular-analysis library by the same author — for file I/O, atom selections, topology and secondary-structure assignment, and renders on eframe/egui + wgpu.","Beyond the basics it leans into the niceties that make a viewer pleasant to live in: screen-space ambient occlusion and real-time cast shadows, VMD-style depth cueing, order-independent transparency, gradient backgrounds, a material picker with live previews, periodic-image replication with dashed wrap-around bonds, and a hover lens that quietly reveals the atoms tucked under a cartoon ribbon or a molecular surface. A settings dialog remembers how you like things between runs."],"features":["Pure Rust, end to end — memory-safe, no segfaults, no manual memory management,","A modern GPU pipeline — atoms and bonds are ray-cast as analytic impostors in","Portable by construction — wgpu targets Vulkan, Metal, DX12 and WebGPU, so the","VMD muscle memory preserved — the same selection language, the same mouse","Cartoon ribbons — a faithful port of VMD's NewCartoon: a per-chain modified Catmull–Rom spline through the Cα trace, a carbonyl-derived ribbon frame with running-average orientation, elliptical cross-sections that morph…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yesint/molar_vis/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"822be54eb02055559ad366871aed0549580fabe63da6cf1818358736cb22f05b","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.413Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.413Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A modern, legacy-free molecular visualizer modeled after VMD, written in pure Rust. The molecule is drawn with hand-written GPU ray-cast impostors (WGSL) and real-time cartoon ribbons — no OpenGL fixed pipeline, no X11, no C/C++/Tcl. It runs natively on Linux, Windows, macOS and compiles to WebAssembly (try it now online).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yesint/molar_vis/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"822be54eb02055559ad366871aed0549580fabe63da6cf1818358736cb22f05b","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yesint/molar_vis/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.415Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T19:16:25Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yesint/molar_vis/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.417Z","hash":"822be54eb02055559ad366871aed0549580fabe63da6cf1818358736cb22f05b","originalBytes":28516,"storedBytes":28516,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["molar","vis","python","selection","one","viewer","live","build","cartoon","molecule","api","browser","color","molecules","atoms","bonds","gpu","representation","same","selections","surface","native","rep","structure","style","molecular","settings","view","vmd","ambient","analysis","frame","geometry","mol","representations","runs","scene","trajectory","window","background","bond","camera","depth","every","file","full","modern","protein","pymolar","rust","scripting","set"